---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalHeader from '../components/LegalHeader.astro';
---

<Layout title="Data Processing Agreement">
  <main class="bg-white">
    <LegalHeader lang="en" />
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 text-text">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Data Processing Agreement</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-10">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 4, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <p>
          This Data Processing Agreement ("DPA") supplements the Tenants10
          <a href="/terms" class="text-primary font-medium">Terms of Service</a> and applies
          automatically whenever you ("Customer") use the Tenants10 Service to process personal
          data of your own occupants, tenants, staff, or other individuals ("Occupant Data") on
          Tenants10's platform. It is intended to meet the requirements of Art. 9 of the Swiss
          Federal Act on Data Protection and, where applicable, Art. 28 GDPR.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">1. Roles</h2>
          <p>
            The Customer is the <strong>controller</strong> of Occupant Data. Tenants10 KIG is
            the <strong>processor</strong>, acting only on the Customer's documented instructions
            as given through the Service's normal configuration and use (e.g. which modules are
            enabled, who the Customer invites, what data the Customer enters).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">2. Subject matter, nature & purpose</h2>
          <p>
            Tenants10 processes Occupant Data to provide the property/facility-management
            functions the Customer configures: tenancy and lease administration, rent and payment
            tracking, maintenance and work order management, compliance/inspection tracking,
            in-app messaging, document storage, and related AI-assisted features (document
            extraction, translation, and in-app assistants), for the duration of the Customer's
            subscription.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">3. Categories of data & data subjects</h2>
          <p>
            Occupant Data may include: name, contact details, lease and payment records,
            maintenance requests, messages, and documents relating to the Customer's tenants,
            occupants, and building contacts. It does not include special categories of
            personal data (e.g. health data) unless the Customer chooses to upload such content,
            which the Customer warrants it has a lawful basis to do.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">4. Sub-processors</h2>
          <p>
            The Customer authorises Tenants10 to engage the sub-processors listed in Section 8 of
            the <a href="/privacy" class="text-primary font-medium">Privacy Policy</a> (as updated
            from time to time) to provide the Service. Tenants10 remains responsible for each
            sub-processor's compliance with data-protection obligations equivalent to those in
            this DPA, and will give the Customer reasonable notice of any new sub-processor that
            processes Occupant Data, so the Customer may object on reasonable data-protection
            grounds.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">5. Security measures</h2>
          <p>
            Tenants10 maintains technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risk,
            including: encryption of data in transit; role-based and building-scoped access
            control within the platform; audit logging of administrative actions; hosting of
            core infrastructure in Microsoft Azure's Switzerland North region; and regular review
            of sub-processor security practices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">6. Confidentiality</h2>
          <p>
            Tenants10 ensures that personnel authorised to process Occupant Data are bound by an
            appropriate duty of confidentiality.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">7. Assistance to the Customer</h2>
          <p>
            Taking into account the nature of the processing, Tenants10 will reasonably assist
            the Customer in responding to data subject requests (access, correction, deletion,
            export) raised by the Customer's own occupants/tenants, and in meeting any applicable
            data-protection impact assessment or breach-notification obligations relating to
            Occupant Data, insofar as the required information is available to Tenants10.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">8. Personal data breach notification</h2>
          <p>
            Tenants10 will notify the Customer without undue delay after becoming aware of a
            personal data breach affecting that Customer's Occupant Data, and will provide
            available information to help the Customer meet its own notification obligations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">9. Return & deletion of data</h2>
          <p>
            On termination of the Customer's subscription, Tenants10 will make Occupant Data
            available for export for a reasonable period, and will then delete or anonymise it,
            except where Tenants10 is required by applicable law (such as Swiss financial
            record-keeping rules) to retain certain records for longer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">10. International transfers</h2>
          <p>
            Where Occupant Data is transferred outside Switzerland or the EEA by a sub-processor
            listed under Section 8 of the Privacy Policy, that transfer is made under standard
            contractual clauses and/or the EU–US / Swiss–US Data Privacy Framework, as applicable
            to that provider.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">11. Audit</h2>
          <p>
            On reasonable written request, and no more than once per year absent a specific
            incident, Tenants10 will provide the Customer with available information
            demonstrating compliance with this DPA, such as a summary of security measures or
            relevant sub-processor certifications.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">12. Precedence & contact</h2>
          <p>
            In the event of a conflict between this DPA and the Terms of Service regarding the
            processing of Occupant Data, this DPA prevails. For a signed/countersigned version of
            this DPA for your own records, or questions about a specific engagement (such as a
            larger facility-management customer with its own data-protection office), contact
            <a href="mailto:support@tenants10.com" class="text-primary font-medium">
              support@tenants10.com
            </a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
